---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
    </head>

    <body>
        <Header />

        <main>
            <!-- Hero -->
            <section class="hero">
                <h1>I TURN COMPLEXITY INTO STRUCTURE</h1>

                <p class="hero-description">
                    Complex systems rarely fail because they're too complex.
                    They fail when nobody understands <strong
                        >what actually matters.</strong
                    >
                </p>

                <p class="hero-description">
                    I help engineering teams make sense of difficult systems,
                    make hard technical decisions, and build software that holds
                    up in the real world.
                </p>

                <a href="#problem">&darr; KEEP READING</a>
            </section>

            <!-- Problem -->
            <section class="problem" id="problem">
                <h2>WHEN EVERYTHING IS CONNECTED, NOTHING IS OBVIOUS</h2>

                <div>
                    <p>
                        Requirements. Constraints. Legacy decisions. Distributed
                        systems. Real-time data. Hardware. Protocols.
                        Performance.
                    </p>

                    <p>Everything affects everything else.</p>

                    <p>And that's where things usually go wrong.</p>

                    <p>
                        <strong
                            >The hardest engineering problems aren't solved by
                            writing more code.</strong
                        >
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        They're solved by understanding the system well enough
                        to know <strong
                            >what code should exist in the first place.</strong
                        >
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Services -->
            <section class="services">
                <h2>
                    I HELP TURN TECHNICAL UNCERTAINTY INTO SOMETHING YOU CAN
                    BUILD
                </h2>

                <div class="service-grid">
                    <article class="service-card">
                        <h3>Architecture &amp; System Design</h3>

                        <p>
                            You have requirements, constraints and a vague idea
                            of where you're going. I turn that into a system
                            with clear boundaries, explicit trade-offs and
                            decisions you can actually build on.
                        </p>
                    </article>

                    <article class="service-card">
                        <h3>Systems Diagnosis</h3>

                        <p>
                            Something works. But nobody really knows why. I dig
                            into difficult existing systems, find the real
                            constraints and separate symptoms from the problems
                            underneath them.
                        </p>
                    </article>

                    <article class="service-card">
                        <h3>Engineering Rescue</h3>

                        <p>
                            The system has become painful. Changes are risky.
                            Performance is unpredictable. Nobody wants to touch
                            certain parts anymore. I help make it understandable
                            again — and give the team a way forward.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Process -->
            <section class="process">
                <h2>I DON'T START WITH TECHNOLOGY</h2>

                <div>
                    <div class="process-flow">
                        <p class="process-step">Ambiguity</p>
                        <p class="process-step">Understanding</p>
                        <p class="process-step">Structure</p>
                        <p class="process-step">Decisions</p>
                        <p class="process-step">Engineering</p>
                        <p class="process-step">Reliable System</p>
                    </div>

                    <p>Because choosing a technology is easy.</p>

                    <p>
                        <strong
                            >Knowing what the system actually needs is the hard
                            part.</strong
                        >
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>
